{"book":19,"chapter":83,"context":{"chapter":83,"title":"Keep Not Silent, O God","summary":"A coalition of ten nations plots to wipe out Israel's name. The people ask God to deal with them as he did with Midian and Sisera, so that all will know the LORD alone is Most High.","background":"Title: 'A Song or Psalm of Asaph.' The last Asaph psalm, a communal lament. No known event matches this exact alliance; some suggest the coalition against Jehoshaphat (2 Chronicles 20). It recalls victories under Deborah and Gideon (Judges 4–8).","customs":[],"watchFor":["The list of nations from Edom to Assyria (vv. 6–8).","The goal is knowledge of God, not just defeat of enemies (v. 18), one of the few places KJV prints 'JEHOVAH.'"],"connections":["Judges 4:15-24","Judges 7:25","Judges 8:21","Exodus 6:3"]},"verses":{"0":{"w":[["שִׁיר","shir","H7892","HNcmsa","a song"],["מִזְמוֹר","mizmor","H4210","HNcmsa","a psalm"],["לְאָסָף","le'asaf","H623","HR/Npm","of Asaph"]]},"1":{"w":[["אֱלֹהִים","'elohim","H430","HNcmpa","O God"],["אַל","'al-","H408","HTn","[let] not"],["דֳּמִי","domi-","H1824","HNcmsa","silence"],["לָךְ","lakh","H9032","HR/Sp2ms","[belong] to you"],["אַל","'al-","H408","HTn","may not"],["תֶּחֱרַשׁ","techerash","H2790","HVqj2ms","you be silent"],["וְאַל","ve'al-","H408","HC/Tn","and may not"],["תִּשְׁקֹט","tishkot","H8252","HVqj2ms","you be inactive"],["אֵל","'el","H410","HNcmsa","O God"]],"x":[[19028001,19028001,6],[19035022,19035022,5],[19050003,19050003,4],[19109001,19109002,3],[23042014,23042014,3]],"xn":5},"2":{"w":[["כִּי","ki-","H3588","HTc","for"],["הִנֵּה","hineh","H2009","HTj","here!"],["אוֹיְבֶיךָ","'oyveikha","H341","HVqrmpc/Sp2ms","enemies your"],["יֶהֱמָיוּן","yehemayun","H1993","HVqi3mp/Sn","they are in an uproar !"],["וּמְשַׂנְאֶיךָ","umesan'eikha","H8130","HC/Vprmpc/Sp2ms","and [those who] hate you"],["נָשְׂאוּ","nase'u","H5375","HVqp3cp","they have lifted"],["רֹאשׁ","rosh","H7218","HNcmsa","a head"]],"x":[[19081015,19081015,5],[23017012,23017012,4],[4002