e of the leaders of David’s choir (1 Chr. 6:39). Psalms 50 and 73-83 inclusive are attributed to him. He is mentioned along with David as skilled in music, and a “seer” (2 Chr. 29:30).","verses":32,"father":"Berechiah","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"moab_2103","name":"Moab","also":"Moabitess, Moabitish, Moabites","summary":"Used to denote the people of Moab (Num. 22:3-14; Judg. 3:30; 2 Sam. 8:2; Jer. 48:11, 13).","verses":149,"father":"Lot","mother":"Daughter of Lot - Older","v":[6]},{"id":"amalek_197","name":"Amalek","also":"","summary":"Dweller in a valley, the son of Eliphaz and grandson of Esau (Gen. 36:12; 1 Chr. 1:36); the chief of an Idumean tribe (Gen. 36:16).","verses":22,"father":"Eliphaz","mother":"Timna","v":[7]},{"id":"ben-ammi_451","name":"Ben-ammi","also":"","summary":"Son of my kindred; i.e., “born of incest”, the son of Lot by his youngest daughter (Gen. 19:38).","verses":2,"father":"Lot","mother":"Daughter of Lot - Younger","v":[7]},{"id":"lot_1830","name":"Lot","also":"","summary":"(Heb. goral, a “pebble”), a small stone used in casting lots (Num. 33:54; Jonah 1:7). The lot was always resorted to by the Hebrews with strictest reference to the interposition of God, and as a method of ascertaining the divine will (Prov. 16:33), and in serious cases of doubt (Esther 3:7).","verses":34,"father":"Haran","mother":"","v":[8]},{"id":"sisera_2757","name":"Sisera","also":"","summary":"The captain of Jabin’s army (Judg. 4:2), which was routed and destroyed by the army of Barak on the plain of Esdraelon. After all was lost he fled to the settlement of Heber the Kenite in the plain of Zaanaim.","verses":17,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"jabin_677","name":"Jabin","also":"","summary":"Another king of Hazor, called “the king of Canaan,” who overpowered the Israelites of the north one hundred and sixty years after Joshua’s death, and for twenty years held them in painful subjection.","verses":6,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"zalmunna_2983","name":"Zalmunna","also":"","summary":"One of the two kings of Midian whom the “Lord delivered” into the hands of Gideon.","verses":9,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"zebah_2997","name":"Zebah","also":"","summary":"Man-killer, or sacrifice, one of the two kings who led the vast host of the Midianites who invaded the land of Israel, and over whom Gideon gained a great and decisive victory (Judg. 8).","verses":9,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"oreb_2255","name":"Oreb","also":"","summary":"Raven, a prince of Midian, who, being defeated by Gideon and put to straits, was slain along with Zeeb (Judg. 7:20-25).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"zeeb_3033","name":"Zeeb","also":"","summary":"The wolf, one of the two leaders of the great Midianite host which invaded Israel and was utterly routed by Gideon.","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]}],"places":[{"id":"edom_357","name":"Edom","kind":"Region","lat":31.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Idumea (Isa. 34:5, 6; Ezek. 35:15). “The field of Edom” (Gen. 32:3), “the land of Edom” (Gen. 36:16), was mountainous (Obad. 1:8, 9, 19, 21).","verses":79,"v":[6]},{"id":"gebal_449","name":"Gebal","kind":"City","lat":34.1191,"lon":35.64614,"summary":"A Phoenician city, not far from the sea coast, to the north of Beyrout (Ezek. 27:9); called by the Greeks Byblos. Now Jibeil.","verses":3,"v":[7]},{"id":"tyre_1184","name":"Tyre","kind":"City","lat":33.26807,"lon":35.20936,"summary":"A rock, now es-Sur; an ancient Phoenician city, about 23 miles, in a direct line, north of Acre, and 20 south of Sidon. Sidon was the oldest Phoenician city, but Tyre had a longer and more illustrious history.","verses":52,"v":[7]},{"id":"asshur_109","name":"Asshur","kind":"City","lat":36.35941,"lon":43.15289,"summary":"Second son of Shem (Gen. 10:22; 1 Chr. 1:17). He went from the land of Shinar and built Nineveh, etc. (Gen. 10:11, 12). He probably gave his name to Assyria, which is the usual translation of the word, although the form Asshur is sometimes retained (Num. 24:22, 24; Ezek. 27:23, etc.).","verses":4,"v":[8]},{"id":"kishon_705","name":"Kishon","kind":"Water (River)","lat":32.76195,"lon":35.0641,"summary":"Winding, a winter torrent of Central Palestine, which rises about the roots of Tabor and Gilboa, and passing in a northerly direction through the plains of Esdraelon and Acre, falls into the Mediterranean at the north-eastern corner of the bay of Acre, at the foot of Carmel.","verses":5,"v":[9]},{"id":"midian_796","name":"Midian","kind":"Region","lat":28.75,"lon":34.75,"summary":"An Arabian tribe descended from Midian. They inhabited principally the desert north of the peninsula of Arabia. The peninsula of Sinai was the pasture-ground for their flocks.","verses":44,"v":[9]},{"id":"en-dor_385","name":"En-dor","kind":"","lat":32.6257,"lon":35.38567,"summary":"Fountain of Dor; i.e., “of the age”, a place in the territory of Issachar (Josh. 17:11) near the scene of the great victory which was gained by Deborah and Barak over Sisera and Jabin (comp. Ps. 83:9, 10).","verses":3,"v":[10]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","TDavid","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[7892,7892,4210,4210,623,623,430,430,408,408,1824,408,408,2790,408,408,8252,410,410],[2009,3588,341,341,1993,8130,8130,8130,5375,5375,7218,7218],[6191,6191,5475,5475,5921,5971,5971,3289,3289,5921,6845,6845,6845],[559,1980,3582,3582,3582,3582,1471,1471,1471,8034,8034,8034,3478,3478,2142,2142,3808,5750],[3588,3820,3820,3820,3289,3289,3162,3772,3772,1285,1285,5921,5921],[168,168,123,123,3459,3459,3459,4124,4124,1905,1905,1905],[1381,1381,5983,6002,6002,6429,6429,5973,3427,3427,6865,6865],[1571,804,3867,3867,5973,1961,2220,1121,1121,1121,3876,3876,5542],[6213,0,0,4080,4080,4080,4080,4080,5516,5516,5516,2985,2985,5158,5158,5158,7028],[8045,8045,5874,5874,1961,1961,1828,1828,127,127,127],[7896,5081,5081,6159,6159,2062,2062,3605,3605,5257,5257,2078,2078,6759,6759],[834,559,3423,3423,3423,0,0,4999,4999,430,430],[7896,7896,1534,15